{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1500633-what-size-are-packs","id":1500633,"title":"What size are packs?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-18T12:12:02-08:00","id":1500633,"title":"What size are packs?","content":"Guessing minimum 3 maximum... 5? 6? 7?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T12:45:43-08:00","id":1500638,"title":"","content":"In terms of just Garou? Probably from about two to a dozen, with no technical upper limit and a tendency towards the lower end.<br /> <br /> If we take a more Forsaken approach and allow both Kinfolk and particularly close human allies to be counted we're likely looking at 10-20 for most packs and a couple of hundred for the largest, with the majority being effectively their support network and family. We can get picky and quibble about who counts, especially as it's not the model that WtA was intended to use, but I honestly find it more useful. A pack of eight Garou with no support will be less effective than a pack of three Garou and two dozen Kinfolk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T13:52:45-08:00","id":1500653,"title":"","content":"3 to 12 (IIRC) is the range the books have given in the past with closer to 5 being the norm. There is no metaphysical cap here, just social pressure (both internally of trying to manage a large pack, and externally to break up into two or three smaller packs) and a game-play matter of keeping the default player character group size in line with expecting player group size.<br /> <br /> Packs can have less than three members, but this is generally considered an unstable situation that will end in the pack disbanding if they can't increase their numbers. If a pack gets destroyed in a battle and only one member survives, their spirit will usually give them some grace period to recruit more members before leaving (or potentially becoming a personal totem instead). In the rare cases were a spirit directly gathers up a pack on their own rather than the pack forming via the Totem Rite, it's kinda unclear when exactly the group counts as a &quot;pack&quot; in a social sense (mechanically it's when everyone buys enough dots in Totem to afford the base cost of the spirit), but what little we've seen of that in the lore of the game tends to lean towards the Garou respecting such an effort as a pack even before they might fully qualify as one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T19:07:30-08:00","id":1500689,"title":"","content":"At maximum, once in the past, packs could be up to 50 (Changing Ways, page 101). The same book also says it's rare to see a pack nowadays with more than 10.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1876,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","user":"Fenixpp","date":". 01-19-2023, 03:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T21:02:30-08:00","id":1500695,"title":"","content":"Fifty is kind of a ridiculous idea as one pack, considering that's a decent sized Sept. I always took that with a grain of salt, since that's basically just a Sept without a Caern if you think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T12:25:39-08:00","id":1500758,"title":"","content":"Oh totally it's indeed ridiculous xD, I tend to interpret it with kinder eyes though since it was in ancient times. No delirium, no populational crisis as of the nowadays Garou, way more space for them to run around, etc...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T15:36:17-08:00","id":1500777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenixpp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1500633-what-size-are-packs?p=1500689#post1500689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At maximum, once in the past, packs could be up to 50 (Changing Ways, page 101). The same book also says it's rare to see a pack nowadays with more than 10.</div> </div> </div> </div>Changing Ways. That does make the whole piece of info quite suspect.<br /> <br /> I'd personally go with packs being 3-10 people usually, with a heavy prevalence of 3-6 members (conveniently about as much as a PC group). However, this also allows for packs to go againt each other and to have competition and oneupmanship and the classic trope of making friends after conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T15:42:59-08:00","id":1500778,"title":"","content":"I was just informing the most recent information on the matter '-'. I wouldn't make a 50 Garou pack for instance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1876-fenixpp","name":"Fenixpp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1876_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T15:43:31-08:00","id":1500779,"title":"","content":"IME packs that are in the ~10 range is much more common in LARPing than TT. If you have a 30 person LARP, it can be a lot to handle 6+ packs. Bigger packs also allow for some redundancy if players can't make every session so in groups where there's a higher expectation of unreliable scheduling, packs tend to tick up a bit too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T16:31:46-08:00","id":1500783,"title":"","content":"I suspect 50+ Garou packs were either from a pre-Cearn period or very rare and only formed in exceptional circumstances. Most likely the former, back when Tribes hadn't formed a Garou's primary social ties would be their packs, which may legitimately have been extended families. They'd likely have been a lot more organic, with members joining up, leaving, and migrating as circumstances demanded.<br /> <br /> Then particularly powerful totems begin drawing multiple Packs to them, and bam! Tribes as multi-pack networks begin to form, with them developing cultures over the next few hundred to thousand years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-19T17:33:38-08:00","id":1500796,"title":"","content":"I typically run packs at being between 4-7 Garou, with 10 being the maximum, usually, and only in areas where the Garou in question are in a city environment (Glass Walkers in Atlanta, Georgia), doing special works (Shadow Lords around Tihuta Pass), or in a wild area (Red Talons in yellowstone). <br /> <br /> 3 could be a good sign that the Pack has been through hell, though! If the pack is running at 3 and has been for a while, it could be a signal the pack has been decimated and unable to recover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27762-jackal-alltrades","name":"Jackal Alltrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T17:45:41-08:00","id":1500889,"title":"","content":"The size of packs is probably best limited to one's span of control. Span of control is the term used to describe the manageable number of direct subordinates a supervisor (the pack leader) can lead. That tends to be around 7 plus or minus 2 (depending on the leader's ability). So most packs maximum number of members are usually between 5 to 9. Now a person can manage more than that, but typically the effectiveness of their leadership declines.<br /> <br /> If you go beyond this, you are probably introducing a greater hierarchy. For example, military squads often number around a dozen people lead by a sergeant. But that sergeant has one or more subordinates (corporals) who take over the direct management of others, thus allowing the sergeant to have an effective span of control. In the US military, we've either seen a push to reduce the squad to a 9 or 10 men team or to break the squad down further into fire teams lead by corporals. Among Garou, this might be emulated by having the &quot;beta&quot; directly lead about half of the pack, allowing the pack leader to directly manage his half of the pack plus the beta. But I don't think many packs get this large. Unlike the military, you have no way of enforcing a hierarchy like that, and I think it would be very common for the &quot;beta&quot; and his team to simply form their own pack. I would think it takes a very special leader and team to make such a large pack work.<br /> <br /> It becomes harder and harder to form consensus in larger groups. And despite Garou being a hierarchical society, that hierarchy is supposed to be based on merit (the Renown system plus Challenges). Garou really don't have some bureaucratic authority over one another, their leadership is based on acceptance of their subordinates. If a subordinate doesn't like the decisions his pack leader makes, that Garou can just leave the pack. Maybe she joins another or forms her own. She might even leave the sept assuming another sept will accept her. It doesn't work that way in the military, and even in business there are barriers to changing positions or even changing companies. <br /> <br /> Packs work best when the members are few enough that the pack leader can develop strong relationships with all members, make them feel part of the same team, and individually convince them to go with the general consensus. In small groups, people can be convinced to go along with something they don't agree for the sake of group harmony. In larger groups, it'd be easier for a disaffected member to convince another disaffected member to leave and form their own group.<br /> <br /> Odd numbers tend to be preferred over even numbers, because odd numbers can produce a majority that can cause the minority to feel like they should go along for the sake of group harmony. If a contentious decision produces an equal split, the other side may not cave in. While a pack leader could force the issue by stating his will decides, any pack leader who finds himself constantly with an equally divided pack will probably see that pack split up. It's better to have a group that easily divides into a majority and minority. But four person packs can definitely work if the pack leader is dominant and the other three get along well.<br /> <br /> For my chronicles, I typically have most NPC packs be between 3 - 5 Garou. At larger caerns with greater sept population, I might have one larger pack of 6-8 members (or if the caern is really big maybe even two or three such packs). I do have the occasional pack be only 2 members, but that is generally frowned upon unless there is a compelling reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}